---
import BlockLayout from '../../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import {
  BEACH_BLANKET_COVERAGE_PATHS,
  BEACH_BLANKET_PROMOTION_CAMPAIGN,
  BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_DISPATCHES,
  BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS,
} from '../../../lib/beach-commons-v8-promotion';

const description =
  'Four copy-ready promotion dispatches, twelve product photographs, a realistic coverage ladder, and public campaign receipts for The Beach Blanket Review.';

const wall = [
  ['ikea-picnic', 'IKEA picnic base'],
  ['cgear-original', 'CGear sand-through floor'],
  ['matador-pocket', 'Matador pocket layer'],
  ['nomadix-festival', 'Nomadix all-rounder'],
  ['kelty-biggie', 'Kelty sunset layer'],
  ['rumpl-everywhere', 'Rumpl waterproof mat'],
  ['slowtide-koko', 'Slowtide cotton square'],
  ['yeti-lowlands', 'YETI single-object room'],
] as const;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'A Blanket Is a Tiny Public Room',
  description,
  datePublished: '2026-07-28',
  dateModified: '2026-07-28',
  mainEntityOfPage: BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.promotionDesk,
  image: BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.socialCard,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Michael Hoydich' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PointCast', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz' },
  about: {
    '@type': 'Article',
    name: 'The Beach Blanket Review',
    url: BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.canonical,
  },
};
---

<BlockLayout
  title="A Blanket Is a Tiny Public Room · Promotion Desk"
  description={description}
  image="/images/og/b/0521.png"
  imageWidth={1200}
  imageHeight={630}
  alternates={[
    {
      type: 'application/json',
      href: '/beach-commons/v8/share.json',
      title: 'The Beach Blanket Review promotion packet',
    },
  ]}
>
  <main class="bbp" data-blanket-promotion>
    <header class="bbp__hero">
      <nav class="bbp__flag mono" aria-label="Promotion desk navigation">
        <a href="/">POINTCAST</a>
        <span>FIELD STUDY 008 / PROMOTION DESK</span>
        <a href="/beach-commons/v8/share.json">JSON ↗</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="bbp__hero-grid">
        <div class="bbp__hero-copy">
          <p class="mono">THE FULL PROMOTIONS POST · JULY 2026</p>
          <h1>A BLANKET<br />IS A TINY<br /><em>PUBLIC ROOM.</em></h1>
          <p>
            Twelve current products. Seven group systems. One exact $99.99 sand kit.
            Zero affiliate dollars. The promotion is the experiment: ordinary shopping
            becomes more interesting when everybody contributes a job.
          </p>
          <div class="bbp__hero-actions mono">
            <a href="/beach-commons/v8">READ THE REVIEW ↗</a>
            <button type="button" data-native-share>SHARE THE ROOM ↗</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bbp__photo-wall" aria-label="Eight products from The Beach Blanket Review">
          {wall.map(([id, label], index) => (
            <figure>
              <img
                src={`/beach-commons/v8/products/${id}.webp`}
                alt={`${label}, maker or merchant photograph used as a credited editorial reference.`}
                width="960"
                height="960"
                loading={index < 2 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'}
              />
              <figcaption class="mono">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {label}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bbp__scoreline mono" aria-label="Campaign facts">
        <span>12 PRODUCTS</span>
        <span>7 SYSTEMS</span>
        <span>$99.99 EXACT SAND KIT</span>
        <span>$0 AFFILIATE EARNED</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="bbp__essay" aria-labelledby="essay-title">
      <p class="mono">THE POST / FULL LENGTH</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="essay-title">You brought a blanket. Did you bring a floor?</h2>
        <p class="bbp__essay-lead">
          Most beach-blanket roundups begin with softness. This one begins by asking what
          job the rectangle is supposed to do.
        </p>
        <p>
          A cotton throw can be lovely over clean legs at sunset and miserable beneath
          four sandy elbows. Pocket nylon can establish a dry boundary almost anywhere
          and provide almost no comfort. A sand-through mat can behave like a brilliant
          floor while still asking somebody else to bring softness. A warm camp blanket
          belongs on top of the system, away from sparks, after the ground problem is solved.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is why The Beach Blanket Review treats each product as one piece of
          temporary social architecture: floor, soft layer, marker, warmth, or portable
          insurance. It then recombines twelve products into seven group systems instead
          of pretending one textile should win every assignment.
        </p>
        <div class="bbp__receipts">
          <article>
            <p class="mono">SYSTEM 01 / EXACT</p>
            <strong>$99.99</strong>
            <h3>The sand kit</h3>
            <p>One six-foot CGear mesh floor plus one Matador pocket-size clean layer.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <p class="mono">SYSTEM 02 / COLOR FIELD</p>
            <strong>$99.96</strong>
            <h3>The IKEA layer lab</h3>
            <p>One repellent picnic base plus three washable throws with four visible jobs.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p>
          The larger experiment is not really about blankets. If ten to twenty people
          each contributed $100 of non-food goods, would they buy ten isolated objects—or
          coordinate a floor, shade, coffee, cups, low light, fire-ring safety, games,
          weaving, sound, and a way to pack every trace home? The receipt becomes a score
          for cooperation.
        </p>
        <p>
          The media experiment matters too. Product photographs remain credited editorial
          references. Prices are dated snapshots. PointCast received no samples, claims no
          hands-on testing, uses no affiliate parameters, and earns $0 from every shopping
          link. Current merchant application routes are reported as possibilities, not
          relationships.
        </p>
        <p>
          So the useful question is not “which blanket wins?” It is: what kind of room are
          we trying to make, who carries which piece, and can the whole thing leave the
          beach cleaner than it found it?
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bbp__dispatches" aria-labelledby="dispatches-title">
      <header class="bbp__section-head">
        <p class="mono">COPY DESK / FOUR CHANNELS</p>
        <h2 id="dispatches-title">One story. Four doors.</h2>
        <p>Each dispatch has a different job. Copy it whole, or open the canonical review and write from the same receipts.</p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        {BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_DISPATCHES.map((dispatch, index) => (
          <li>
            <article class="bbp__dispatch">
              <a class="bbp__dispatch-art" href={dispatch.href}>
                <img src={dispatch.image} alt={dispatch.alt} width="960" height="960" loading="lazy" />
                <span class="mono">{dispatch.channel} / {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              </a>
              <div class="bbp__dispatch-copy">
                <p class="mono">{dispatch.label} · {dispatch.id}</p>
                <h3>{dispatch.headline}</h3>
                <p>{dispatch.copy}</p>
                <blockquote>{dispatch.shareCopy}</blockquote>
                <div class="bbp__dispatch-actions mono">
                  <button type="button" data-copy-dispatch={index}>COPY {dispatch.channel.toUpperCase()} POST</button>
                  <a href={dispatch.href}>{dispatch.cta.toUpperCase()} ↗</a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="bbp__status mono" data-share-status aria-live="polite">Copy desk ready.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="bbp__coverage" aria-labelledby="coverage-title">
      <header class="bbp__section-head">
        <p class="mono">COVERAGE LADDER / NO MAGIC SYNDICATION BUTTON</p>
        <h2 id="coverage-title">How the story could travel beyond PointCast.</h2>
        <p>
          Yahoo is possible, but the honest route is a creator or content-partner
          application—not pretending a paid wire placement is editorial coverage. The
          strongest next move depends on evidence, image rights, and audience size.
        </p>
      </header>
      <ol>
        {BEACH_BLANKET_COVERAGE_PATHS.map((path, index) => (
          <li>
            <article>
              <div class="bbp__coverage-rank mono">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
              <div>
                <p class="mono">{path.lane} · {path.fit}</p>
                <h3>{path.outlet}</h3>
                <p><strong>Route:</strong> {path.route}</p>
                <p><strong>Angle:</strong> “{path.angle}”</p>
                <p class="bbp__coverage-boundary">{path.boundary}</p>
              </div>
              <a class="mono" href={path.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OPEN OFFICIAL PATH ↗</a>
            </article>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="bbp__pitch" aria-labelledby="pitch-title">
      <div>
        <p class="mono">THE FIRST PITCH / USE AFTER ORIGINAL FIELD PHOTOS EXIST</p>
        <h2 id="pitch-title">Four people. One hundred dollars. One floor.</h2>
      </div>
      <blockquote>
        <p><strong>Subject:</strong> PITCH: What four people can build from one $100 beach-floor budget</p>
        <p>
          A beach blanket is usually reviewed as a soft object. I want to report it as a
          tiny room: a ground layer, a clean top, an anchor plan, and a shared carrying
          assignment. Four people will test two exact PointCast systems at a Southern
          California beach, document what stayed dry and put, weigh the packed load, time
          setup and cleanup, and photograph the sand and moisture left in each layer.
        </p>
        <p>
          The service story will separate current manufacturer specifications from our
          original field observations, disclose that the first PointCast edition carried
          plain non-affiliate links, and close with a reusable four-person checklist rather
          than declaring one universal winner.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Do not send this as a performance pitch until the field test and original
        photography exist. Today’s publishable angle is the design exercise and the
        transparent media method.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bbp__proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
      <div>
        <p class="mono">PUBLIC RECEIPTS</p>
        <h2 id="proof-title">The promotion keeps its own ledger.</h2>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt class="mono">CAMPAIGN</dt><dd>{BEACH_BLANKET_PROMOTION_CAMPAIGN.id}</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="mono">PLACEMENT</dt><dd>{BEACH_BLANKET_PROMOTION_CAMPAIGN.placement}</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="mono">MEASUREMENT</dt><dd>{BEACH_BLANKET_PROMOTION_CAMPAIGN.tracking}</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="mono">AFFILIATE REVENUE</dt><dd>$0</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <nav class="mono" aria-label="Campaign proof links">
        <a href={BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.canonical}>REVIEW</a>
        <a href={BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.machineEdition}>MACHINE EDITION</a>
        <a href={BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.pressFiling}>PRESS FILING</a>
        <a href={BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.block}>BLOCK 0521</a>
        <a href={BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.campaignReceipt}>CAMPAIGN RECEIPT</a>
        <a href={BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_LINKS.campaignReport}>LIVE COUNTS</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="bbp__proof-boundary mono">
        OFFICIAL POINTCAST MATERIAL · NOT INDEPENDENT COVERAGE · NO LIVE EVENT · NO MERCHANT SPONSOR · NO AFFILIATE TRACKING
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script
    id="blanket-promo-dispatches"
    type="application/json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify(BEACH_BLANKET_PROMO_DISPATCHES)}
  />
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  <script>
    const root = document.querySelector('[data-blanket-promotion]');
    const payload = document.querySelector('#blanket-promo-dispatches');
    const status = root?.querySelector('[data-share-status]');
    let dispatches: Array<{ shareCopy: string; headline: string; channel: string }> = [];

    try {
      dispatches = JSON.parse(payload?.textContent || '[]');
    } catch {
      dispatches = [];
    }

    async function copyText(text: string) {
      if (navigator.clipboard?.writeText) {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        return;
      }
      const area = document.createElement('textarea');
      area.value = text;
      area.style.position = 'fixed';
      area.style.opacity = '0';
      document.body.append(area);
      area.select();
      document.execCommand('copy');
      area.remove();
    }

    root?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-dispatch]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const index = Number(button.dataset.copyDispatch);
        const dispatch = dispatches[index];
        if (!dispatch) return;
        try {
          await copyText(dispatch.shareCopy);
          if (status) status.textContent = `${dispatch.channel} post copied to the clipboard.`;
          const prior = button.textContent;
          button.textContent = 'COPIED';
          window.setTimeout(() => {
            button.textContent = prior;
          }, 1800);
        } catch {
          if (status) status.textContent = 'Copy was blocked. Select the post text directly.';
        }
      });
    });

    root?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-native-share]')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const first = dispatches[0];
      if (!first) return;
      if (navigator.share) {
        try {
          await navigator.share({
            title: 'A Blanket Is a Tiny Public Room',
            text: first.headline,
            url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/beach-commons/v8',
          });
          if (status) status.textContent = 'The tiny public room left the desk.';
          return;
        } catch {
          // A dismissed native sheet falls through to a useful clipboard copy.
        }
      }
      try {
        await copyText(first.shareCopy);
        if (status) status.textContent = 'LinkedIn post copied to the clipboard.';
      } catch {
        if (status) status.textContent = 'Share was blocked. Use the canonical review link.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</BlockLayout>

<style>
  :global(body:has(.bbp)) { background: #d9c25a; }
  .bbp, .bbp * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .bbp {
    --paper: #f1e7c9;
    --sand: #d9c25a;
    --ink: #16201b;
    --blue: #173f59;
    --red: #d84b35;
    --foam: #edf0e8;
    min-height: 100vh;
    color: var(--ink);
    background:
      repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(22, 32, 27, 0.025) 0 1px, transparent 1px 5px),
      var(--paper);
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
  }
  .bbp a { color: inherit; }
  .mono {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .bbp__hero { color: var(--foam); background: var(--blue); }
  .bbp__flag {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
    padding: 18px clamp(18px, 4vw, 58px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
  }
  .bbp__flag a { text-decoration: none; }
  .bbp__flag a:last-child { text-align: right; }
  .bbp__hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(330px, 0.86fr) minmax(520px, 1.14fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 76px);
    padding: clamp(42px, 7vw, 100px) clamp(18px, 4vw, 58px);
  }
  .bbp__hero-copy { align-self: center; }
  .bbp__hero-copy > p:first-child { color: #f2d45a; }
  .bbp h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 30px;
    font-size: clamp(62px, 8vw, 124px);
    line-height: 0.79;
    letter-spacing: -0.07em;
  }
  .bbp h1 em { color: #f2d45a; font-weight: inherit; }
  .bbp__hero-copy > p:not(:first-child) {
    max-width: 36rem;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 25px);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .bbp__hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .bbp__hero-actions a,
  .bbp__hero-actions button {
    padding: 13px 15px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    color: var(--blue);
    background: #f2d45a;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .bbp__hero-actions button { color: var(--foam); background: transparent; }
  .bbp__photo-wall {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    align-self: stretch;
    border: 1px solid rgba(237, 240, 232, 0.7);
  }
  .bbp__photo-wall figure { position: relative; min-width: 0; margin: 0; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid rgba(237, 240, 232, 0.3); }
  .bbp__photo-wall img { width: 100%; height: 100%; min-height: 220px; display: block; object-fit: cover; filter: saturate(0.9) contrast(1.03); }
  .bbp__photo-wall figcaption {
    position: absolute;
    inset: auto 7px 7px;
    padding: 5px 7px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: rgba(242, 212, 90, 0.9);
    font-size: 7px;
  }
  .bbp__scoreline {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid currentColor;
  }
  .bbp__scoreline span { padding: 14px clamp(12px, 2vw, 28px); border-right: 1px solid currentColor; text-align: center; }
  .bbp__scoreline span:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .bbp__essay {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 100px);
    padding: clamp(70px, 10vw, 150px) clamp(18px, 7vw, 120px);
  }
  .bbp__essay > p { color: var(--red); }
  .bbp__essay > div { max-width: 860px; }
  .bbp__essay h2,
  .bbp__section-head h2,
  .bbp__pitch h2,
  .bbp__proof h2 {
    margin: 0 0 30px;
    font-size: clamp(43px, 6vw, 86px);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 0.94;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  }
  .bbp__essay > div > p { font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 24px); line-height: 1.65; }
  .bbp__essay-lead { font-size: clamp(27px, 3vw, 42px) !important; line-height: 1.3 !important; }
  .bbp__receipts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1px; margin: 50px 0; background: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .bbp__receipts article { padding: clamp(22px, 4vw, 46px); background: var(--sand); }
  .bbp__receipts strong { display: block; margin: 18px 0 6px; color: var(--red); font-size: clamp(58px, 7vw, 100px); line-height: 0.85; letter-spacing: -0.06em; }
  .bbp__receipts h3 { margin: 16px 0 8px; font-size: 26px; }
  .bbp__receipts p:last-child { line-height: 1.5; }
  .bbp__dispatches { padding: clamp(70px, 9vw, 130px) clamp(18px, 5vw, 80px); color: var(--foam); background: var(--ink); }
  .bbp__section-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.35fr 1fr 0.65fr; gap: 30px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 50px; }
  .bbp__section-head > p:first-child { color: #f2d45a; align-self: start; }
  .bbp__section-head > p:last-child { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .bbp__dispatches ol,
  .bbp__coverage ol { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .bbp__dispatch { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr); border-top: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .bbp__dispatch-art { position: relative; min-width: 0; min-height: 470px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bbp__dispatch-art img { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; object-fit: cover; }
  .bbp__dispatch-art span { position: absolute; inset: 12px auto auto 12px; padding: 7px 9px; color: var(--ink); background: #f2d45a; }
  .bbp__dispatch-copy { min-width: 0; padding: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px); border-left: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .bbp__dispatch-copy > p:first-child { color: #f2d45a; }
  .bbp__dispatch-copy h3 { margin: 18px 0; font-size: clamp(35px, 4vw, 62px); font-weight: 400; line-height: 0.95; }
  .bbp__dispatch-copy > p:not(:first-child) { max-width: 44rem; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .bbp__dispatch-copy blockquote {
    max-height: 270px;
    margin: 30px 0 0;
    padding: 20px;
    overflow: auto;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--foam);
    white-space: pre-line;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .bbp__dispatch-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .bbp__dispatch-actions button,
  .bbp__dispatch-actions a {
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border: 1px solid #f2d45a;
    color: #f2d45a;
    background: transparent;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .bbp__dispatch-actions button:hover,
  .bbp__dispatch-actions a:hover { color: var(--ink); background: #f2d45a; }
  .bbp__status { margin: 18px 0 0; color: #f2d45a; }
  .bbp__coverage { padding: clamp(70px, 9vw, 130px) clamp(18px, 5vw, 80px); background: var(--sand); }
  .bbp__coverage .bbp__section-head > p:first-child { color: var(--red); }
  .bbp__coverage li { border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .bbp__coverage article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr auto; gap: clamp(22px, 4vw, 54px); align-items: start; padding: 30px 0; }
  .bbp__coverage-rank { color: var(--red); font-size: 26px; }
  .bbp__coverage article h3 { margin: 8px 0 20px; font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 54px); font-weight: 400; }
  .bbp__coverage article p { max-width: 780px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .bbp__coverage-boundary { padding: 12px; border-left: 4px solid var(--red); background: rgba(241, 231, 201, 0.6); }
  .bbp__coverage article > a { padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid currentColor; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; }
  .bbp__pitch { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 100px); padding: clamp(70px, 9vw, 130px) clamp(18px, 7vw, 120px); background: var(--paper); }
  .bbp__pitch > div > p { color: var(--red); }
  .bbp__pitch blockquote { margin: 0; padding: clamp(25px, 4vw, 55px); color: var(--foam); background: var(--blue); font-size: clamp(17px, 1.8vw, 23px); line-height: 1.6; }
  .bbp__pitch > p { grid-column: 2; margin: 0; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--red); color: var(--red); line-height: 1.5; }
  .bbp__proof { padding: clamp(70px, 9vw, 130px) clamp(18px, 7vw, 120px); color: var(--foam); background: var(--blue); }
  .bbp__proof > div > p { color: #f2d45a; }
  .bbp__proof dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1px; margin: 40px 0; background: var(--foam); border: 1px solid var(--foam); }
  .bbp__proof dl > div { padding: 20px; background: var(--blue); }
  .bbp__proof dt { color: #f2d45a; }
